  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-26T21:42:18.556Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The approach to acessibility is literally one that prefers to pretend that disabled user's don't actually exist until enough of them complain about your lack of support.\nMaybe you should just add the basic acessibility features available in most games already, without having disabled players need to compete in this popularity contest wherein they need to garner enough votes to get their needs implemented?\nIt's like your literally making an entire school vote on whether funds should go to a wheelchair ramp or the cash being distributed to everyone with no conditions. Sure the majority will be happen but the disabled users' will be left behind because the other option was more 'popular' than their needs being accomodated.\nHow this isn't seen as unfair is beyond me.",
